==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|ready|ness}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛdinəs/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-readiness.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhyme|en|ɛdinəs|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# The state or degree of being [[ready]]; [[preparedness]].
#: {{ux|en|'''readiness''' for civil emergencies}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|passage=We expressed our '''readiness''', and in ten minutes were in the station wagon, rolling rapidly down the long drive, for it was then after nine. We passed on the way the van of the guests from Asquith.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=February|author=R. C. Riley|title=The London-Birmingham services - Past, Present and Future|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=99|text=[[Euston]] is so traditionally a part of the London scene that many will lament the passing of the old station when rebuilding is complete in '''readiness''' for the new electric service, which will probably be by multiple-units between Euston and [[Wolverhampton]].}}
# [[willingness|Willingness]].
#: {{ux|en|his '''readiness''' to help}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=18 Dec 76|volume=4|number=25|journal=Gay Community News|page=18|author=Tommi Avicolli|title=Previn's Bleak Book Has Note of Hope|text=It was a long, enduring scream — one that would send her back into a time and into a childhood which had been forgotten with the '''readiness''' that we forget unpleasant moments in our lives.}}

